adventurer.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve. Production 2D pixel game sprite pose atlas, edit the supplied approved seed character into ONE full pose sheet. Reference image: same green hooded leather-armored dagger adventurer. Preserve exact outfit colors, facial identity, proportions and pixel cluster style. All poses face RIGHT. Output transparent background, landscape 1536x1024, EXACT 4 equal columns by 2 equal rows = 8 slots, one full body per slot, no overlap, same character size, same grounded bottom baseline and root position relative to each cell. No labels, grid lines, scenery or shadows.
Reading order:
1 relaxed ready idle with dagger;
2 subtly inhaled idle, shoulder raised slightly, cloth follows, same planted feet;
3 attack anticipation: knees bent, torso twisted, dagger drawn back;
4 attack contact: strong forward lunge, leading leg extended, dagger thrust/slash forward to right (wizard thrusts staff forward);
5 spell charge: upright firm stance, free hand lifted, dagger raised preparing energy;
6 spell release: arm and dagger point forward to right, robe/cape swept back, no projectile or VFX (added in game);
7 potion lift: weapons lowered/stowed, free hand holds a SMALL RED potion bottle below face;
8 potion sip: bottle tilted to mouth, head slightly back, same boots firmly planted.
Make changed joint poses clear and readable, especially elbows/shoulders/weapon angles. DO NOT just duplicate the idle with offsets. Same camera scale in all 8 slots. Leave margins for weapon, no cut off tips. Crisp pixel art, no text, no watermark, genuinely transparent alpha.

